Technical Specification E.1.1 (Delay-Tolerant Networking).

For future work, DTN protocols such as Bundle Protocol v7 with custody transfer may be applicable. The key challenge is maintaining belief-state validity when observations are delayed by up to 22 minutes.

Proposition E.1.1 (Belief Staleness). Under communication delay $\tau$, the belief state $b_t$ is based on observations up to time $t - \tau$. The expected drift in belief state over delay $\tau$ is bounded by:

\mathbb{E}[\|b_t - b_{t-\tau}\|_1] \leq 2(1 - \lambda_{\min}^\tau)

where $\lambda_{\min}$ is the minimum eigenvalue of the transition matrix $T$.

Proof sketch. The belief state evolves according to the transition dynamics. Over $\tau$ timesteps, the mixing rate is governed by the spectral gap of $T$. The $\ell_1$ distance between belief states is bounded by the mixing rate. $\blacksquare$

Recommendation: Treat as future work, not as a contribution of this thesis.

